WEBVTT

00:01.630 --> 00:05.880
Vermilio confronts Helck
about whether he can fight his old friends.

00:05.880 --> 00:08.380
This prompts Helck to open up
about his motives,

00:08.380 --> 00:11.080
explaining that he feels obligated
to put a stop to his fellow humans.

00:11.080 --> 00:13.330
Meanwhile, at Castle Urum,

00:13.330 --> 00:16.000
the winged knights gather
to launch yet another attack.

00:16.710 --> 00:19.210
Azudra arrives in the middle of the fierce battle,

00:19.210 --> 00:21.170
and uses his overwhelming power

00:21.170 --> 00:24.880
to fend off the horde of winged knights
in the blink of an eye.

00:50.420 --> 00:52.670
A crazed cog in the machine

00:52.670 --> 00:55.330
Lets loose a shrill cry

00:55.330 --> 00:57.330
Destined for battle and foaming at the mouth

00:57.330 --> 01:00.170
As if waiting for an opening

01:00.420 --> 01:02.540
I got dealt a dangerous card

01:02.540 --> 01:05.170
But prediciments are opportunities

01:05.170 --> 01:07.080
There's no way in hell I'm giving up

01:07.080 --> 01:09.960
The last one standing is the winner

01:10.170 --> 01:12.330
Let's just dance hand in hand

01:12.330 --> 01:15.080
With the grinning devil

01:15.080 --> 01:17.330
No need to care about appearances

01:17.330 --> 01:19.670
Courage trembles with fury

01:19.670 --> 01:22.630
Before the darkness can consume it all

01:22.830 --> 01:23.500
Break it

01:23.500 --> 01:25.000
Kick it away

01:25.000 --> 01:28.080
It's your common sense that'll be smashed to bits

01:28.080 --> 01:32.580
Ignite a flame in the soul that no one can extinguish

01:32.880 --> 01:38.290
This prayer that I now offer to the endless world

01:38.290 --> 01:43.040
Will never stop until the day comes when it gets answered

01:43.040 --> 01:44.710
Always burning

01:44.710 --> 01:47.580
It's my soul

01:55.040 --> 01:59.960
<b>The Human King</b>

02:09.630 --> 02:12.330
H-he's unbelievably strong...

02:18.000 --> 02:19.710
Those tree roots are crazy!

02:20.040 --> 02:22.830
Has Lord Azudra always been this powerful?

02:23.670 --> 02:25.960
It's all thanks to his special ability.

02:25.960 --> 02:29.420
Lord Azudra has the power to
freely manipulate any of the Empire's trees,

02:29.420 --> 02:32.040
included the ones planted here.

02:32.380 --> 02:35.210
It doesn't matter if their leaves fall
off or their trunks give way,

02:35.210 --> 02:37.250
it's possible as long as the roots are left.

02:37.250 --> 02:42.130
Lord Azudra claims that he's the
absolute weakest among the Four Elite Lords,

02:42.330 --> 02:45.670
but I'm of the mind that he's stronger
than any of the other Elite Lords

02:45.670 --> 02:48.460
so long as he's in a place
where these trees are growing.

02:49.330 --> 02:51.290
One of the Four Elite Lords?

02:51.290 --> 02:52.290
Indeed.

02:52.290 --> 02:54.420
We are merely citizens of the Empire.

02:54.420 --> 02:57.750
Even the two places that you've attacked so far,
Castle Thor and Castle Urum,

02:57.750 --> 02:59.750
are nothing more than a fraction of the Empire.

02:59.750 --> 03:03.210
So, there are even more powerful demons
above this guy?

03:03.210 --> 03:05.420
I guess laying waste to them
isn't going to be so easy,

03:05.420 --> 03:08.960
even with our newly awakened hero powers.

03:11.290 --> 03:13.880
I'd really prefer to avoid killing you.

03:13.880 --> 03:17.500
So if you could just go ahead and surrender,
that'd be great.

03:19.040 --> 03:22.080
You sound nothing at all like a demonkin.

03:22.540 --> 03:27.040
Because from what we've been told,
your kind are supposed to be ruthless and evil.

03:31.880 --> 03:33.790
I hope you make the smart choice.

03:38.540 --> 03:39.580
Isty?

03:39.580 --> 03:41.790
I'm sensing... another presence nearby!

03:41.790 --> 03:42.710
Huh?

03:47.540 --> 03:48.170
What the...

03:49.290 --> 03:51.250
Another enemy force?! But where are they?!

03:51.790 --> 03:53.710
There! On the castle walls!

04:09.880 --> 04:11.170
Oh man, there's a lot of them!

04:11.170 --> 04:13.290
Everybody will just have to protect themselves!

04:13.290 --> 04:15.540
Please leave the protecting to me!

04:15.540 --> 04:19.000
W-wait, they're not aiming for us!

04:21.000 --> 04:23.080
They're aiming at the other winged knights!

04:28.170 --> 04:30.830
What's the deal? Are they on our side?

04:31.170 --> 04:32.630
It's just like what happened last time.

04:32.630 --> 04:33.540
Huh?

04:33.540 --> 04:35.630
We had their leader
on the ropes in Castle Urum,

04:35.630 --> 04:38.380
but then he was suddenly killed
by one of their own knights!

04:41.380 --> 04:43.330
Whoa! They've disappeared!

04:52.040 --> 04:54.630
What exactly is happening here?

04:55.080 --> 04:58.630
Well, you're too much of a damn softie
to actually kill us.

04:59.670 --> 05:02.170
So it's a good thing we made sure
to have insurance.

05:02.170 --> 05:03.920
Getting captured would ruin our plans.

05:03.920 --> 05:04.790
Dammit...

05:05.080 --> 05:07.880
We couldn't even eliminate
one of them before the end.

05:07.880 --> 05:10.420
But we did make some progress.

05:10.420 --> 05:13.000
That's more than enough for this run.

05:13.580 --> 05:14.670
"This run"?

05:14.670 --> 05:17.210
I won't deny that
you demon bastards are strong.

05:17.420 --> 05:20.670
These hero powers didn't do much
to stop you from kicking our asses.

05:21.040 --> 05:24.290
But even the mightiest of kingdoms
is bound to crack

05:24.290 --> 05:27.000
under the pressure of an endless assault.

05:27.750 --> 05:30.500
By fighting and accumulating experience
upon the battlefield,

05:30.500 --> 05:32.960
we humans can grow remarkably stronger.

05:33.380 --> 05:36.290
There may still be a gap in strength
between us for now,

05:36.580 --> 05:40.790
but the day will come when we wield power
that's far beyond any of you scum!

05:40.790 --> 05:44.710
I don't get the impression this is merely
a final show of courage before death...

05:45.000 --> 05:46.170
Impossible!

05:46.330 --> 05:47.420
You can't mean...

05:48.420 --> 05:50.960
There is no such thing as death for us!

05:52.250 --> 05:55.080
Because heroes are reborn over and over!

06:05.330 --> 06:06.380
Look!

06:06.380 --> 06:09.420
The winged knights
are turning all floaty and stuff!

06:09.960 --> 06:11.960
Their bodies are vanishing.

06:12.330 --> 06:14.960
So, it seems the lack
of corpses from earlier

06:14.960 --> 06:18.380
wasn't just because
they all got sucked into the gate.

06:22.330 --> 06:24.420
They're really gonna get resurrected, huh?

06:24.420 --> 06:25.960
Human shitheads.

06:25.960 --> 06:27.670
And they have the nerve
to call us the monsters.

06:48.000 --> 06:50.710
Ah, my heroes.

06:52.290 --> 06:55.460
How pitiful it is to see you
come back in defeat.

06:57.290 --> 07:00.380
My sincere apologies, Your Majesty.

07:00.380 --> 07:02.880
The demonkin are a ruthless and evil race.

07:02.880 --> 07:06.330
This world will face devastation
if we leave them unchecked.

07:06.670 --> 07:10.250
That is why you must exterminate them
as quickly as possible.

07:10.880 --> 07:12.750
Now go, my heroes!

07:13.040 --> 07:16.170
Reclaim true peace for the world!

07:17.880 --> 07:20.500
Wh-what the heck is all this?

07:20.500 --> 07:22.330
I was just randomly wandering around,

07:22.330 --> 07:25.000
but somehow I ended up
right in the middle of the hornet's nest!

07:25.250 --> 07:27.830
Why do all these winged knights
keep popping up?

07:28.130 --> 07:30.790
I thought humans went through
an awakening process to create them.

07:30.790 --> 07:33.250
But this makes it seem like
they're being summoned...

07:40.630 --> 07:43.960
Taking a good look, there are all
different kinds of winged knights.

07:44.960 --> 07:47.170
They must be getting ready
for a war council.

07:47.170 --> 07:49.960
Which means I should be able
to get my hands on some juicy info!

07:51.380 --> 07:52.630
But...

07:52.630 --> 07:55.540
sneaking in is going to be very dangerous.

07:55.540 --> 07:57.500
I might have to reconsider.

07:57.920 --> 07:59.080
No, I gotta go!

08:01.790 --> 08:02.750
So that's...

08:04.580 --> 08:06.540
the Human King.

08:08.960 --> 08:11.710
Sorry that I put you guys in a tough spot.

08:11.710 --> 08:15.130
But your willingness to face danger and
prevent the spread of monsters around here

08:15.130 --> 08:16.500
is most appreciated.

08:18.210 --> 08:20.130
Come now, raise your heads!

08:20.130 --> 08:22.380
You don't have to act so formal around me.

08:22.380 --> 08:23.210
Oh yeah?

08:23.210 --> 08:24.080
Hey!

08:26.710 --> 08:28.540
Does that feel better?

08:28.710 --> 08:30.750
This is a quasi-barrier stone.

08:30.750 --> 08:32.210
Although it doesn't last for very long,

08:32.210 --> 08:36.540
it can fend off the toxin of the land
and prevent you from losing any stamina.

08:36.540 --> 08:39.920
All right, everyone!
We're no longer in any danger.

08:39.920 --> 08:42.540
So please take a moment to rest
and enjoy a cup of coffee.

08:42.540 --> 08:43.790
I'm down for that!

08:43.790 --> 08:45.750
Please give me something sweet.

08:48.830 --> 08:50.130
Plunk.

08:50.290 --> 08:52.960
So, Isty, I take it that you passed the test?

08:52.960 --> 08:55.000
Mhm. It was awhile ago, actually.

08:55.000 --> 08:56.960
Would it have killed you to let me know?

08:56.960 --> 09:00.710
How was I supposed to get in touch with you
when I had no idea where you even were?

09:01.000 --> 09:02.290
Fair point.

09:02.540 --> 09:04.380
Anyway, congratulations.

09:04.500 --> 09:05.830
Thank you!

09:06.830 --> 09:08.330
How heartwarming.

09:09.000 --> 09:10.040
Asta!

09:10.250 --> 09:13.210
Lord Azudra!
Asta is trying to make a report!

09:13.210 --> 09:14.210
Very well.

09:14.210 --> 09:16.500
Then you should drink my cup of coffee!

09:19.250 --> 09:21.540
What a relief. You're still alive.

09:21.750 --> 09:23.750
Is everything okay?
You're not going overboard?

09:23.750 --> 09:25.540
Yeah. I'm fine.

09:25.540 --> 09:27.710
Nobody has found me yet.

09:28.920 --> 09:30.830
I've got some major info for you this time!

09:33.170 --> 09:34.290
Is that her ability?

09:34.290 --> 09:35.170
That's right.

09:35.170 --> 09:38.080
She can talk remotely with
her older sister over long distances.

09:44.210 --> 09:46.420
Based on what Asta witnessed
in the human realm,

09:46.670 --> 09:50.080
it's all but certain that the winged knights
have been resurrected.

09:51.790 --> 09:54.210
That seems to be the case.
Most impressive.

09:54.210 --> 09:55.210
That's all he has to say?!

09:55.210 --> 09:58.670
Wh-what are we going to do?!
This is a pretty grave situation, you know!

09:58.670 --> 10:00.540
Now, now. Just settle down.

10:00.540 --> 10:02.790
It's important to keep our wits about us
in times like these.

10:02.790 --> 10:04.330
Y-yes, but...

10:04.330 --> 10:07.130
For starters, let's take stock
of the current situation.

10:07.130 --> 10:07.960
Okay then!

10:07.960 --> 10:10.630
It's time to start the
emergency military discussion!

10:10.630 --> 10:12.080
Aren't we out of place here?

10:12.080 --> 10:12.830
Be quiet.

10:12.830 --> 10:14.040
Feel free to eat and drink.

10:14.040 --> 10:16.540
First up, please take a look at this!

10:17.420 --> 10:20.830
This is a list of all the problems the
eastern region is currently dealing with.

10:20.830 --> 10:23.750
They've been organized in order of importance.

10:24.080 --> 10:26.460
Number one! Ms. Anne is MIA!

10:26.460 --> 10:28.500
Number two! The human menace!

10:28.500 --> 10:31.000
Number three!
Fending off the monsters to the east!

10:31.000 --> 10:33.170
Number four!
The absence of the Demon Lord!

10:33.170 --> 10:35.750
And finally, number five!
The Hero Helck!

10:34.000 --> 10:35.710
<b>Illustrated by Rococo</b>

10:35.920 --> 10:37.460
Why did they include Helck in there?

10:37.460 --> 10:39.210
Helck seems awfully low on the list...

10:39.790 --> 10:42.330
For the sake of our military strength
and my mental health,

10:42.330 --> 10:45.920
finding number one
is our utmost priority at the moment.

10:45.920 --> 10:48.670
But I'd like to discuss the humans
before we get to that.

10:48.670 --> 10:50.710
Please take a look at this chart!

10:50.710 --> 10:54.630
It shows the ranking of all the nearby powers
that threaten the Empire as a whole!

10:54.630 --> 10:55.960
The northern powers!

10:55.130 --> 10:57.830
<b>Northern Region</b>

10:55.960 --> 10:57.830
Their threat rank is triple S!

10:57.830 --> 11:01.540
<b>Capital</b>

10:57.830 --> 11:01.540
<b>Western Region</b>

10:57.840 --> 11:01.540
<b>Southern Region</b>

10:58.080 --> 11:01.540
The western and southern powers!
Their threat ranks are both C!

11:01.540 --> 11:03.080
The eastern powers!

11:01.540 --> 11:08.960
<b>Eastern Region</b>

11:03.080 --> 11:05.420
Specifically the human kingdom,
which has been ranked E.

11:05.420 --> 11:08.540
However, this rank only applies during
the periods when they have no hero.

11:09.000 --> 11:12.830
In regards to monsters, the rank of
New-World Lifeforms ranges from B to S.

11:12.830 --> 11:16.000
While regular monsters
can be from C to A rank.

11:16.630 --> 11:18.750
The humans are ranked way too low...

11:19.290 --> 11:21.080
As you already know,

11:21.080 --> 11:24.670
human beings are the weakest
out of all races that exist in the world.

11:25.000 --> 11:28.790
So long as we watched out for their hero,
they weren't really a force to be concerned about.

11:29.130 --> 11:30.460
That being said...

11:31.080 --> 11:34.540
if all the human soldiers
have been awakened as heroes,

11:34.540 --> 11:36.130
then their threat rank...

11:36.580 --> 11:38.580
would probably be about a C.

11:39.080 --> 11:41.630
Uh-huh. C rank, you say?

11:41.630 --> 11:42.880
Warrior Hyura.

11:43.500 --> 11:45.380
You've engaged them in battle.

11:45.380 --> 11:47.630
How high would you
estimate their combat levels to be?

11:47.630 --> 11:49.290
Well, let me think.

11:49.290 --> 11:53.330
The most common type with
those bulky bodies are about 30.

11:53.330 --> 11:55.830
Then I'd say their leader was around 35.

11:55.830 --> 11:56.790
Exactly.

11:56.790 --> 11:59.460
And at that level,
they aren't a big problem for us.

11:59.460 --> 12:01.040
But unfortunately,

12:01.040 --> 12:03.380
they can be resurrected after being killed.

12:04.250 --> 12:07.580
When you take that into account,
their threat rank becomes A.

12:07.750 --> 12:10.920
Huh? That's still lower
than I would have expected...

12:10.920 --> 12:12.750
Just give it some thought.

12:13.080 --> 12:14.790
The fact of the matter is,

12:14.790 --> 12:17.880
we already fight against monsters
that spawn infinitely on a daily basis.

12:17.880 --> 12:20.330
Oh, that makes sense!

12:20.330 --> 12:21.210
Except...

12:21.210 --> 12:25.040
that's under the assumption humans will
never develop any more than they already have.

12:25.630 --> 12:27.790
But after awakening as heroes,

12:27.790 --> 12:29.710
they are bound to grow stronger.

12:30.880 --> 12:32.960
And if every single human

12:32.960 --> 12:36.290
were to reach the same peak form
as the heroes of the past did,

12:36.290 --> 12:37.670
then their threat rank would be...

12:38.130 --> 12:40.130
higher than triple S.

12:41.580 --> 12:43.710
A bigger threat than the northern forces...

12:44.170 --> 12:48.670
More than half of the Empire's troops are
currently posted at the northern defense line.

12:49.130 --> 12:52.210
Which means if the humans continue
to develop and strengthen their army

12:52.210 --> 12:54.170
until it's on par with the north...

12:54.830 --> 12:58.500
then we won't have enough troops
left to hold them off.

12:59.540 --> 13:01.830
And that will spell the end for all of us.

13:02.920 --> 13:04.420
The Empire will perish.

13:05.580 --> 13:08.250
Then a new world will be born in its place.

13:11.670 --> 13:14.710
This is heavy stuff.
I guess I gotta be ready to fight, too.

13:14.710 --> 13:16.420
It's really problematic.

13:16.420 --> 13:20.130
How do you put a stop to an enemy that revives
no matter how many times you beat them?

13:20.380 --> 13:24.000
Don't forget they mentioned something
about growing stronger with each fight.

13:24.000 --> 13:27.830
So we have to think carefully before engaging them
in battle or it might make the situation worse.

13:28.750 --> 13:31.250
We can't win by just defeating the humans.

13:31.750 --> 13:35.920
We need to find another way to deal with them,
otherwise the situation is hopeless.

13:36.250 --> 13:37.920
Yes. That's exactly right.

13:37.920 --> 13:39.210
Which is why I propose...

13:39.500 --> 13:42.880
that our strategy should be
to nullify their ability to resurrect.

13:43.380 --> 13:44.920
We can do that?!

13:44.920 --> 13:46.290
Yes, of course.

13:46.290 --> 13:47.540
Huh?!

13:47.880 --> 13:51.830
There is no such thing in this world as life
that is born disconnected from death.

13:51.830 --> 13:54.500
Their ability to resurrect
must come from a magic spell.

13:55.250 --> 13:58.460
All we have to do is defeat the spellcaster
and then their spell will be undone.

13:58.460 --> 13:59.500
A spellcaster?

13:59.500 --> 14:00.750
Do you mean...

14:00.750 --> 14:01.710
Indeed.

14:02.420 --> 14:04.210
The Human King.

14:10.960 --> 14:12.420
Once we defeat their king,

14:12.790 --> 14:15.420
the humans won't be able
to resurrect any longer.

14:15.420 --> 14:17.960
B-but how do you know that for sure?

14:18.920 --> 14:21.330
Well, I haven't lived
all these centuries for nothing!

14:21.630 --> 14:23.710
This is a story from a long time ago,

14:23.710 --> 14:26.380
but I once fought against a hero
who was capable of reviving.

14:27.420 --> 14:31.250
It struck me as odd, so I did a lot
of digging to figure out the cause.

14:31.250 --> 14:33.960
And I ultimately learned that it was
the result of the king's magic.

14:34.380 --> 14:37.710
Based on what Agent Asta
reported seeing in the human realm,

14:37.710 --> 14:40.630
I'm almost positive it must be
the same spell at work this time.

14:41.630 --> 14:44.500
The king's magic works
in roughly the same way

14:44.500 --> 14:47.880
that the Deep Green Contract
I used for the tournament did.

14:48.580 --> 14:50.710
By forging a contract with the king,

14:50.710 --> 14:53.250
heroes can gain
the ability to be resurrected.

14:53.250 --> 14:56.380
But the spell only works
on an awakened hero.

14:56.380 --> 15:00.960
The effects after being cast include:
resurrection at the foot of the king upon death.

15:00.960 --> 15:04.250
And absolute obedience to the king,
or something like that.

15:05.000 --> 15:09.000
It's quite similar to the magic that I use,
except much more powerful.

15:09.000 --> 15:12.330
But even the king should still be
no more than an ordinary human.

15:12.330 --> 15:15.420
So how is it possible for them
to use such a highly advanced magic?

15:15.420 --> 15:19.250
Obviously, it's not something they can achieve
merely by having the title of "king."

15:19.250 --> 15:23.170
Which means they must be another type
of awakened being that's akin to the hero.

15:23.170 --> 15:24.710
Another type?

15:25.000 --> 15:27.170
If we classify the hero as a combat type,

15:27.170 --> 15:30.000
then the king is a support type
who can draw out their strength.

15:30.000 --> 15:34.210
And considering that their hero was gifted
with physical prowess on par with our own,

15:34.210 --> 15:35.630
then it's not unreasonable to think

15:35.630 --> 15:38.290
a human with magic power
surpassing ours could be born as well.

15:40.000 --> 15:43.170
D-do we really stand
a chance of beating their king?

15:44.750 --> 15:46.830
We just have to give it our best shot!

15:46.830 --> 15:48.290
Seriously?

15:48.290 --> 15:50.460
But there's something else
we have to do before that.

15:50.460 --> 15:52.170
Shore up our defenses.

15:52.380 --> 15:54.880
Per the info that Agent Asta gathered,

15:54.880 --> 15:57.830
the humans will be making another
march on Castle Urum with their forces

15:57.830 --> 15:59.580
the day after tomorrow.

16:00.290 --> 16:02.290
We're going to fend them off.

16:02.670 --> 16:04.580
Then, we'll focus on retaking Castle Thor.

16:04.580 --> 16:09.880
<b>"Castle Thor"</b>

16:05.250 --> 16:07.830
Control of that stronghold is
necessary whether we're attacking

16:06.670 --> 16:09.880
<b>"Castle Urum"</b>

16:06.670 --> 16:09.880
<b>"Land of Humans</b>

16:06.670 --> 16:09.880
<b>Border Fortress"</b>

16:07.830 --> 16:09.290
or defending against the humans.

16:09.920 --> 16:12.880
Securing those two victories will be
our first order of business.

16:13.330 --> 16:15.630
After we solidify our defenses,
formulate a strategy,

16:15.630 --> 16:17.920
and make sure that
everything else is in order,

16:17.920 --> 16:19.710
then we'll dispatch
an elite unit of warriors

16:19.710 --> 16:22.040
with the mission of vanquishing
the Human King.

16:24.170 --> 16:26.630
Get your butts in gear! No slacking!

16:26.630 --> 16:28.330
Come on! We gotta hurry!

16:28.330 --> 16:30.500
Or else the humans are gonna
be raining hell on our doorstep!

16:30.500 --> 16:31.710
Yessir!

16:31.710 --> 16:33.880
Hold that thought,
I just realized that it's lunchtime!

16:33.880 --> 16:35.000
Yessir!

16:35.250 --> 16:36.420
Quit working!

16:36.420 --> 16:37.460
Yessir!

16:37.460 --> 16:38.630
Go wash your hands!

16:38.630 --> 16:40.080
Yessir!

16:40.460 --> 16:43.080
Man, this has become
a pretty crazy fiasco, huh?

16:43.080 --> 16:44.580
You can say that again.

16:44.580 --> 16:48.250
Ya know, I'm not really into
the whole "fighting" thing.

16:48.630 --> 16:51.080
Really wish I understood
why it had to come to this...

16:51.080 --> 16:52.830
That's a question for the humans.

16:52.830 --> 16:54.750
Maybe we can make it like
the Demon Lord tournament

16:54.750 --> 16:57.130
and just challenge them
to a bunch of weird contests!

16:57.130 --> 17:01.210
But if we were to lose those,
would that make accepting death any easier?

17:01.210 --> 17:04.540
Would you just stand by and watch
your fellow demonkin get slaughtered?

17:05.960 --> 17:07.500
Are those hands squeaky clean?!

17:07.500 --> 17:08.960
Yessir!

17:08.960 --> 17:10.130
Nope, can't do it.

17:10.130 --> 17:12.040
You need to steel yourself.

17:12.880 --> 17:15.000
Did you tell her not to overdo it?

17:15.000 --> 17:16.960
Yeah. Except...

17:17.210 --> 17:18.960
Sure, I won't push myself too hard!

17:18.960 --> 17:22.670
But if there's a time to pull out all the stops,
then I think this it!

17:22.670 --> 17:24.380
So I'm gonna do my best!

17:24.380 --> 17:26.880
I think it kinda had the opposite effect.

17:26.880 --> 17:28.670
That's Asty for you.

17:29.290 --> 17:31.920
I just knew I should have gone with her!

17:31.920 --> 17:34.580
Except that would ruin the whole advatange
of using you two.

17:34.580 --> 17:36.170
You're not wrong, but...

17:36.170 --> 17:37.630
It's all right.

17:37.630 --> 17:40.040
I'm the one who trained Asty.

17:40.210 --> 17:42.210
So I know she won't go down easily.

17:43.670 --> 17:45.790
Anyway, I guess Asta was right.

17:46.040 --> 17:49.540
We can't afford to spare any effort
until Lady Vermilio comes back.

17:49.540 --> 17:50.540
Yep.

17:50.540 --> 17:52.000
Let's do our best.

17:53.790 --> 17:55.920
So, this is where the gate was.

17:55.920 --> 17:58.210
What exactly are we doing here,
Lord Azudra?

17:58.710 --> 18:02.420
The passageway created by the gate
won't have completely disappeared just yet.

18:02.420 --> 18:04.210
Which means if we reopen the gate,

18:04.210 --> 18:07.250
the destination on the other side should
be the same place that Vermikins ended up at.

18:07.250 --> 18:10.920
W-wait, so you're going to where Lady Vermilio
is by opening the gate again?

18:10.920 --> 18:14.500
Unfortunately, it's impossible for me
right now to create a gate big enough

18:14.500 --> 18:16.210
for someone to pass through.

18:16.380 --> 18:18.710
Huh? Then why did we come here?

18:18.710 --> 18:21.080
To help Vermikins, of course!

18:21.500 --> 18:24.170
I want to do whatever is possible
while we have the chance.

18:24.170 --> 18:25.630
And what would that be?

18:25.630 --> 18:27.130
You'll find out soon.

18:27.130 --> 18:29.880
Hon! Hold onto these and stand back!

18:29.880 --> 18:31.330
Wh-what's all this?

18:31.580 --> 18:33.500
The Deep Green Pathfinder!

18:33.500 --> 18:36.420
It's a magic wand that can point her
in the direction of the Empire.

18:36.790 --> 18:38.420
The Deep Green Letter!

18:38.420 --> 18:40.000
It's just a regular letter.

18:40.000 --> 18:41.500
I wrote some words
of encouragement for her

18:41.500 --> 18:43.830
along with an explanation on the effects
of my Deep Green magic.

18:44.040 --> 18:44.960
A mandarin orange!

18:44.960 --> 18:48.170
Vermikins' favorite food.
It should give her some peace of mind.

18:48.630 --> 18:51.580
Making a gate big enough for people
to pass through is out of the question,

18:52.380 --> 18:55.380
but creating one that's
small enough for some items...

18:55.380 --> 18:57.040
shouldn't be a problem for me!

19:00.420 --> 19:02.750
Wow! It's a little gate!

19:02.750 --> 19:03.880
Awesome! I did it!

19:03.880 --> 19:05.710
Hon! Throw the items into the gate!

19:05.710 --> 19:06.790
Okay!

19:06.790 --> 19:08.420
Move quickly,
it won't hold for very long!

19:08.420 --> 19:09.580
Are you done yet?!

19:09.960 --> 19:11.380
I'm all done!

19:16.540 --> 19:19.250
Are you okay, Lord Azudra?

19:20.290 --> 19:22.460
I was on the verge of blacking out...

19:22.460 --> 19:26.670
I never imagined that spatial-teleportation magic
would put so much strain on the body!

19:26.880 --> 19:28.540
Nobody should be using that spell

19:28.540 --> 19:30.710
unless they have the ability
to resurrect themselves later.

19:31.630 --> 19:33.000
Lord Azudra...

19:33.580 --> 19:35.250
But it all worked out.

19:35.250 --> 19:37.290
Hopefully she'll pick them up.

19:37.290 --> 19:41.830
Anyway, it's pretty pathetic that
an Elite Lord of the Empire such as myself

19:41.830 --> 19:43.710
can't manage to do any better than this.

19:44.710 --> 19:47.460
All right, now let's get
to repairing the barrier stone.

19:47.750 --> 19:49.420
We don't have time for any breaks.

19:49.420 --> 19:50.420
Please just rest for a moment, Lord Azudra!

19:50.420 --> 19:52.540
Ugh, nope... can't feel my legs...
Please just rest for a moment, Lord Azudra!<b></b>

19:52.540 --> 19:54.250
Ugh, nope... can't feel my legs...

20:02.290 --> 20:03.750
Something's over there!

20:10.500 --> 20:11.580
Yummy!

20:13.960 --> 20:17.460
I gotta say, it's actually nice to do things
the hard way from time to time.

20:25.460 --> 20:27.290
This pales in comparison to Helck's cooking!

20:27.290 --> 20:29.880
But why?!
Does he use some secret ingredient?!

20:29.880 --> 20:32.080
Mm! That smells great!

20:32.500 --> 20:34.380
Let me have a taste, too!

20:35.290 --> 20:37.080
I-it's not ready yet, fool!

20:37.080 --> 20:38.130
Just a little?

20:38.130 --> 20:40.460
You'll just have to wait over there
until I'm satisfied with it!

20:40.460 --> 20:41.540
Alrighty.

20:41.540 --> 20:43.420
I'm really looking forward to it!

20:44.630 --> 20:45.880
Jeez...

20:47.040 --> 20:48.750
The fire is about to go out...

20:49.330 --> 20:50.500
I'm back!

20:50.500 --> 20:51.830
Took you long enough.

20:51.830 --> 20:52.920
What kept you?

20:52.920 --> 20:55.170
There was a yummy fruit lying over there!

20:55.170 --> 20:56.920
Don't waste time
eating scraps off the ground!

20:56.920 --> 20:59.170
We need to hurry
or the fire will go out.

20:59.380 --> 21:02.830
I swore to myself that I wouldn't use
any magic to cook this dish.

21:02.830 --> 21:04.670
Which means at this rate,
the soup will never be done!

21:07.080 --> 21:08.000
Here!

21:11.000 --> 21:12.540
What was that paper you just threw in?

21:12.540 --> 21:13.830
I dunno!

21:19.830 --> 21:22.630
I promise you

21:22.630 --> 21:25.580
Someday when the world

21:25.580 --> 21:27.670
Comes to an end

21:27.670 --> 21:30.290
I hope we meet once again

21:42.380 --> 21:47.750
Someone once told me

21:47.750 --> 21:53.670
You were like a flower

21:53.670 --> 21:59.210
In a room without water, yet surely

21:59.210 --> 22:01.710
Blooming towards tomorrow

22:03.420 --> 22:06.210
If it was all a dream

22:06.210 --> 22:09.080
To know you

22:09.080 --> 22:12.000
To be in love

22:12.000 --> 22:15.500
I wouldn't know the meaning of life

22:16.330 --> 22:19.130
Even if tomorrow

22:19.130 --> 22:21.830
The rain pours

22:21.830 --> 22:24.210
Dawn will come and

22:24.210 --> 22:27.290
Rainbows will arch over the world

22:27.670 --> 22:30.380
The pain in my heart

22:30.380 --> 22:33.250
The tears trickling down

22:33.250 --> 22:36.710
Let's turn it into seeds for the future

22:36.710 --> 22:38.330
We go on

22:39.040 --> 22:41.080
Until our clumsy love

22:41.080 --> 22:44.250
Blooms into a flower

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>Next Episode</b>

22:46.040 --> 22:50.830
<b>Back to the Continent</b>

22:46.710 --> 22:49.040
Next time: "Back to the Continent"
